TypeRegistry duplicate detection broken for T field

#### Description

When registering multiple TypeSpec instances with the same T field, the duplicate detection logic fails to properly identify conflicts. The registry allows registration of specs with duplicate T values when it should reject them.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "ariga.io/atlas/schemahcl"
)

func main() {
    registry := &schemahcl.TypeRegistry{}

    spec1 := &schemahcl.TypeSpec{
        Name: "first",
        T:    "duplicate_t",
    }

    spec2 := &schemahcl.TypeSpec{
        Name: "second", 
        T:    "duplicate_t",  // Same T as spec1
    }

    // This should fail but doesn't
    err := registry.Register(spec1, spec2)
    if err != nil {
        fmt.Printf("Expected error: %v\n", err)
    } else {
        fmt.Println("Registration succeeded when it should have failed")
    }
}
```

The registration succeeds when it should return an error about duplicate T values. The duplicate check appears to be checking the wrong field or using incorrect logic.

Slice parsing fails for pointer element types

#### Description

When parsing environment variables into slices with pointer element types (e.g., `[]*string`), the parsing fails with a panic about type assignment.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "os"
    "github.com/caarlos0/env/v11"
)

type Config struct {
    Items []*string `env:"ITEMS"`
}

func main() {
    os.Setenv("ITEMS", "item1,item2,item3")

    cfg := Config{}
    if err := env.Parse(&cfg); err != nil {
        fmt.Printf("Error: %v\n", err)
        return
    }

    fmt.Printf("Parsed items: %v\n", cfg.Items)
}
```

This code panics with:
```
panic: reflect.Set: value of type string is not assignable to type *string
```

The issue occurs when trying to parse comma-separated values into a slice where the elements are pointers to basic types.

